  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shaikh Nisar Vajir Alias Tamboli vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 July, 2025 923-ABA-1248-2025.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1248 Of 2025 Shaikh Nisar Vajir alias Tamboli Versus The State of Maharashtra ------------------------- Ms. Ranjita R. Barhate for the Applicant. Mrs. M. L. Sangit, App for the State. ------------------------- Coram : Advait M. Sethna, J. Date : 23 July 2025 P. C.: 1.",
    "facts": "The FIR is lodged on 22 October 2024 at 17:13 hours by the Pachod Police Station, Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar (Rural). The date of occurrence of the alleged incident as stated in the FIR is 21 October 2024. The FIR has been registered under Sections 30(2)(a), 27(3)(e), 26(2)(iv), 26(2)(ii) and 26(2)(i) of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Sections 123, 275, 274 and 223 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (\"BNS\"). that the issues involved are connected to the various other Applications which have been filed in this Court concerning possession/supply/storage of the banned substances i.e. Gutka in its various forms. As far as the present Application is concerned, it is stated that the Applicant's name is not ascribed in the FIR, however, surfaced from the statement of co-accused persons during the investigation. It is alleged that the Applicant has supplied the contraband to the accused persons, who have allegedly purchased it from the Applicant. In such view of the matter, this appears to be covered in order passed in Anticipatory Bail Application No.857 of 2025 and connected proceedings. Learned Advocate for the Applicant would submit that the two accused persons as named in the FIR are enlarged on regular bail by the trial Court.",
    "arguments": "",
